ed). We could argue that B's memory issue could be mitigated, and his nasty remarks are concerning but can be addressed with training. Also note lack of evidence on decision quality for B, but his conscientiousness suggests good judgment. We could also note that B's technical competence includes weather assessment and computer skills, which are important for long-distance flights.\n\nThus we will state we continue to recommend B, summarizing why B remains best, acknowledging concerns, and perhaps propose next step: maybe we need to verify B's decision-making record. But we should keep it concise.\n\nWe must output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
